# Success Criteria

Genesis is successful when:

- no significant engineering knowledge is lost
- engineering conversations become reusable knowledge
- repository history becomes engineering understanding
- design evolution becomes design intelligence
- engineering failures become recovery knowledge
- architectural evolution becomes organizational memory
- every completed mission improves future missions
- the Chief Agent demonstrates measurable engineering improvement over time

---

# Long-Term Outcome

The Chief Agent should eventually possess a richer understanding of KoreLumina than any individual contributor.

Not because it replaces human expertise.

Because it continuously preserves, connects, and applies the collective engineering experience of the organization while remaining governed by human leadership.

The construction of KoreLumina becomes the permanent foundation of the Chief Agent's engineering education.
